a-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/484cb392-8feb-4475-b667-865bc63d1b2a.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1941\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>8\n\n[underlined: Absolute Privilege]\n\n[underlined: White] (cont)\n\nByron would not ever require a\nshowing of necessity or need. It is\nhard to think of a criminal case\nin which this can be shown &amp; equally\nhard for Byron to imagine a\ncriminal case in which [underlined: in camera]\nexam should not be allowed. Only\n17(c) is required to get to [underlined: in camera].\nBut if one gets to an [underlined: in camera]\nprocedure, then Byron would accept\nthe CADC screening procedure.\nIf we require more than 17(c) as\npredicate to [underlined: in camera], Byron says\nhe [struck: illegible] doesn&#x27;t find enough in record\nbefore us to affirm.\n\n[underlined: Marshall] (affirm)\n\nProsecutor is entitled to any evidence\nthat 17(c) entitles him to. Pres\nhas no special privilege.\n\n[underlined: Blackmun] (affirm)\nAgrees with Byron\nNo reason for a broad const.\ndecision. (See his memo).\nWants a [struck: illegible] pragmatic, narrow\ndecision based on special facts.\nDo not get into waiver.\nAgrees in large part with Douglas.\n\n[underlined: Powell] (affirm)\n(See my memo. which I used at Conference)\n\nPotter [struck: illegible] agrees with me that\n• 17(c) is inadequate standard. Brennan would\naccept my Part III; Potter might (does agree Privilege is\nConstitutional).</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1973 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>United States v. Nixon, President of the United States, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></spa